    "evidence_text": "One Lucky Elephant\n\nPardon Mon Affaire\n\n It was remade as the 1984 American film \"The Woman in Red\".\n\nTori Kelly\n\nElephant (2003 film)\n\nElephant is a 2003 drama film edited, written and directed by Gus Van Sant.\n\n The film stars mostly new or non-professional actors, including John Robinson, Alex Frost, and Eric Deulen.\n\nJim Fields\n\nJames Wallace Fields (born September 1958) is an American film director, producer, playwright and actor.\n\n2003 Cannes Film Festival\n\n French opera and theatre director, filmmaker, actor and producer Patrice Ch\u00e9reau was the President of the Jury.\n\n The Palme d'Or went to the American film \"Elephant\" by Gus Van Sant based on the Columbine High School massacre.\n\nChristine Yoo is a Korean-American writer, director, producer and filmmaker.\n\n For the film, Yoo also received a Best Director award at the Atlanta Korean Film Festival as well.\n\nNeil LaBute\n\n He also directed several episodes for shows such as \"Hell on Wheels\" and \"Billions\".\n\nChristopher B. Landon\n\nWhispers: An Elephant's Tale\n\n It was co-written, co-produced and directed by Dereck Joubert.",
